-- title:
--   Kronecker's theorem — the line $t\mapsto t\tau \bmod \mathbb Z^N$ is dense in $\mathbb T^N$ iff $\tau_1,\dots,\tau_N$ are $\mathbb Q$-linearly independent
-- statement:
--   **Kronecker's theorem for linear flows on the torus.** Let $N\ge 0$ be an integer, let $\mathbb T=\mathbb R/\mathbb Z$ be the circle group and $\mathbb T^N$ the $N$-dimensional torus with the product topology. For a vector $\tau=(\tau_1,\dots,\tau_N)\in\mathbb R^N$ let
--   $$\overline\gamma_\tau\colon\mathbb R\to\mathbb T^N,\qquad \overline\gamma_\tau(t)=(t\tau_1,\dots,t\tau_N)\bmod \mathbb Z^N,$$
--   be the continuous one-parameter subgroup of $\mathbb T^N$ generated by $\tau$. Then
--   $$\overline\gamma_\tau(\mathbb R)\ \text{is dense in}\ \mathbb T^N\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad \tau_1,\dots,\tau_N\ \text{are linearly independent over}\ \mathbb Q .$$
--
--   This is the case $d=N$ of Theorem B.5.2.1(1) of the source together with its converse, which is also contained in that theorem: if the $\mathbb Q$-span of the coordinates of $\tau$ has dimension $d<N$, the closure of the orbit is a $d$-dimensional subtorus, hence a proper subset of $\mathbb T^N$. The source recalls the statement at the end of §B.5.1 ("when $\tau_1,\dots,\tau_N$ are $\mathbb Q$-linearly independent, $\overline\gamma_N$ is [...] with dense image") and says that this is the only case of the Kronecker–Weyl theorem it requires; it is the starting point of the equidistribution statement (B.5.2.1) and of the strong recurrence of reciprocal finite Euler products (Proposition B.5.3.3).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The index set $\{1,\dots,N\}$ is an arbitrary finite type `ι` (so $N=0$ is allowed). $\mathbb T$ is Mathlib's `UnitAddCircle = AddCircle (1 : ℝ)`, the coercion `ℝ → UnitAddCircle` is the quotient map $\mathbb R\to\mathbb R/\mathbb Z$, and $\mathbb T^N$ is `ι → UnitAddCircle` (Mathlib's `UnitAddTorus ι`) with the product topology; $\overline\gamma_\tau(t)$ is written inline as `fun k => ((t * τ k : ℝ) : UnitAddCircle)`. The source's additional claim in §B.5.1 that $\overline\gamma_N$ is injective is false for $N=1$ and is not part of this statement.
-- source:
--   A. M. Masullo, The Music of the Primes, draft of 20 November 2026, https://math216.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/the-music-of-the-primes.pdf, p. 627, §B.5.1 (last paragraph) and Theorem B.5.2.1(1); classical reference: B. Hasselblatt and A. Katok, A First Course in Dynamics. With a Panorama of Recent Developments, Cambridge University Press, 2003, Part 1, Theorem 4.1.15 and §4.1.6 (of which the source's theorem is the multi-dimensional version); P. Humphreys, The Summatory Function of Liouville's Function and Pólya's Conjecture, BPh thesis, Australian National University, 2010, §4.3, proof of Lemma 4.3 (general case, as cited by the source)

import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace KroneckerWeyl

theorem denseRange_torusFlow_iff {ι : Type*} [Finite ι] (τ : ι → ℝ) :
    DenseRange (fun t : ℝ => fun k : ι => ((t * τ k : ℝ) : UnitAddCircle)) ↔
      LinearIndependent ℚ τ := by sorry

end KroneckerWeyl
